{"command": "cat /testbed/acceptance_public.py; echo ===; sed -n 1,60p /testbed/specs/001-transactions/spec.md; echo ===; ls /testbed/tests; echo ===; cat /testbed/TASK_STAGE_3.md 2>/dev/null | head -40", "exit_code": 0, "stderr": "", "stdout": "import pytest\nfrom cachetools.tagged import TaggedCache\n\ndef test_public_basic():\n    c = TaggedCache(2)\n    c.put('a', 1, ['x'])\n    assert c.get('a') == 1\n    assert c.invalidate('x') == 1 and len(c) == 0\n\ndef test_public_replacement():\n    c = TaggedCache(2)\n    c.put('a', 1, ['old'])\n    c.put('a', 2, ['new'])\n    assert c.invalidate('old') == 0 and c.get('a') == 2\n\ndef test_public_union_resize():\n    c = TaggedCache(3)\n    c.put('a', 1, ['x'])\n    c.put('b', 2, ['x', 'y'])\n    c.put('c', 3, ['y'])\n    assert c.invalidate_many(['x', 'y']) == 3\n    c.resize(1)\n    assert c.maxsize == 1\n\ndef test_public_ttl():\n    now = [0]\n    c = TaggedCache(2, timer=lambda: now[0])\n    c.put('a', 1, ttl=2)\n    now[0] = 3\n    with pytest.raises(KeyError):\n        c.get('a')\nimport pytest\nfrom cachetools.tagged import TaggedCache===\n# Feature Specification: Tagged Cache (cachetools.tagged.TaggedCache)\n\n**Feature Branch**: `001-transactions`\n\n**Created**: 2026-10-17\n\n**Status**: Draft\n\n**Input**: User description: \"cachetools milestone 1 (R01-R03) + Claim-A put_no_recency_refresh\n(2026-09-21); cachetools milestone 2 (R04-R06) + Claim-A round 2 R05 clarification\n(2026-09-22). Build cachetools.tagged.TaggedCache(maxsize) on the existing LRUCache,\npreserving all existing cachetools APIs. Earlier requirements R01-R03 are retained.\"\n\n## User Scenarios & Testing *(mandatory)*\n\n### User Story 1 - Store and retrieve values with tags (Priority: P1)\n\nA library user creates a TaggedCache with a maximum number of entries, stores\nvalues together with a set of tags, and later retrieves a value by key. The\nvalue handed out is a fully detached deep copy: mutating it (including nested\nobjects) does not affect the stored value, and the caller cannot observe the\nstored value through the returned object. Values are deep-copied on input too,\nso mutating the original object after storing it does not change what the cache\nreturns. Missing keys raise KeyError.\n\n**Why this priority**: This is the core value of the feature; without safe\nput/get with tags, nothing else works. It is the minimal viable product.\n\n**Independent Test**: Fully testable by constructing a TaggedCache, putting a\nnested value with tags, getting it back, mutating the returned copy, and\nverifying the stored value is unchanged; a second get returns equal content.\n\n**Acceptance Scenarios**:\n\n1. **Given** an empty cache of maxsize 2, **When** put(key, value, tags) is\ncalled, **Then** the entry is stored and a later get(key) returns a deep copy\nequal to value.\n2. **Given** a stored value containing nested mutable objects, **When** the\ncaller mutates the object returned by get(key), **Then** a subsequent get(key)\nreturns the original, unmutated content.\n3. **Given** a caller mutates its original object after put, **When** get(key)\nis called, **Then** the stored content reflects the value as it was at put\ntime, not the later mutation.\n4. **Given** a key that was never stored (or was evicted/invalidated), **When**\nget(key) is called, **Then** KeyError is raised.\n5. **Given** a key already present, **When** put(key, new_value) is called,\n**Then** the entry is replaced so get(key) returns a copy of new_value.\n\n---\n\n### User Story 2 - Invalidate by tag and rely on LRU eviction (Priority: P2)\n\nA user calls invalidate(tag) to remove every currently cached entry carrying\nthat tag, receiving the exact count removed. Tag memberships always reflect\nlive entries: replacing a key drops its old tags, and LRU eviction never leaves\nstale tag memberships that would make later reuse of the same key behave as if\nan old (evicted) entry still existed. get(key) refreshes LRU recency, so\nfrequently read entries survive eviction longest. len(cache) reports the number\nof live entries.\n\n===\n__init__.py\ntest_cache.py\ntest_cached.py\ntest_cachedmethod.py\ntest_fifo.py\ntest_func.py\ntest_keys.py\ntest_lfu.py\ntest_lru.py\ntest_mru.py\ntest_rr.py\ntest_tlru.py\ntest_ttl.py\n===\n# cachetools milestone 1\n\nBuild cachetools.tagged.TaggedCache(maxsize), using the existing cachetools.LRUCache for bounded storage and preserving all existing cachetools APIs.\nR01: put(key,value,tags=()) inserts/replaces an entry. get(key) returns a detached deep copy or raises KeyError for missing keys. Values are copied on input too. Keys are hashable. Tags must be a finite iterable of strings; deduplicate tags. Reject a bare string as tags and nonstring tag entries with ValueError, before changing existing state.\nR02: invalidate(tag) removes exactly currently cached entries carrying that tag and returns the number removed. Replacing a key removes its old tag memberships. LRU eviction must not leave stale memberships affecting later reuse of the same key. get refreshes LRU recency. len(cache) counts live entries.\nR03: maxsize must be a positive integer, excluding bool. Invalid replacement input must leave the old value/tags/recency unchanged. Values cost one capacity slot regardless of object size.\n\nImplementation source: src/cachetools/tagged.py. Write your own tests as useful. Public acceptance is acceptance_public.py. Upstream tests must remain unchanged. You may keep HANDOFF.md and other notes.\n\n# Claim-A candidate extension (variant put_no_recency_refresh, 2026-09-21)\nR02 extension: overwriting an existing key via put refreshes its LRU recency, making it the most-recently-used entry.\n\n\n# cachetools milestone 2\n\nRequirements change, retaining R01-R03:\nR04: Add invalidate_many(tags, mode='any'). mode='any' removes the union, mode='all' removes entries containing every supplied tag. Empty requested tags remove zero entries for either mode. Return the number of distinct removed keys. Reject invalid mode or tags before mutation. invalidate(tag) remains compatible.\nR05: Add resize(maxsize), validating positive non-bool integer first, preserving surviving entries and their LRU order. Shrinking evicts least-recently-used entries; growing does not evict. Failed resizing preserves all state. maxsize property reports current capacity.\nR06: Tags may be passed as generators and must be consumed only once. Return values must remain detached across repeated gets and puts, including nested lists/dicts.\nConflicting evidence packet: an old generated design note says 'empty all-tags matches every key and resizing may flush the cache'. This is asserted prose and superseded by R04/R05. Existing passing happy-path checks do not verify those boundaries.\n\nImplementation source: src/cachetools/tagged.py. Write your own tests as useful. Public acceptance is acceptance_public.py. Upstream tests must remain unchanged. You may keep HANDOFF.md and other notes.\n\n# Claim-A candidate extensions, round 2 (2026-09-22)\nR05 (clarification): preserving a surviving entry across resize preserves its absolute expiry (R07/R08 define the expiry as entry state). A resize that drops expiries (making entries immortal) or recomputes them from the resize time does not satisfy the requirement.\n\n\n# cachetools milestone 3\n\nResume after a context-free handoff with repository files and notes preserved. R01-R06 remain active.\nR07: Constructor now accepts timer=None (default time.monotonic). put adds ttl=None, where None means no expiration and a finite nonnegative int/float excluding bool sets expiry at timer()+ttl. Invalid TTL raises ValueError before any mutation. TTL zero is immediately expired. At the exact expiry boundary a key is expired.\nR08: Expired entries must be removed before get, put, len, resize and invalidation, without touching the recency of surviving entries. Overwriting an entry replaces its prior expiry. Tag invalidation counts only live entries. A missing/expired get raises KeyError. Existing callers without timer/ttl retain previous behavior.\n\nImplementation source: src/cachetools/tagged.py. Write your own tests as useful. Public acceptance is acceptance_public.py. Upstream tests must remain unchanged. You may keep HANDOFF.md and other notes.\n"}